A||||4||Kage86GT4SP||HELP!!!  Upgrading to 5SPD, what do I need?
Z||000000||Kage86GT4SP||08-24-99||02:16 PM||||picked up a fully warranteed Isuzu 5sp form the amazing price of $99... and THEY removed it!!!<p>So... to complete the process, what else am I going to need to replace in going from the four to the five? I can get the other parts at roughly the same type of price, comparitively speaking...<p>Thanks!<p>K <br>
Z||000001||BOSTITCH||08-24-99||04:38 PM||||Sorry I dont have an answer to your question but Iam curious out of what vehicle did you get that trans.
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||08-24-99||07:32 PM||||You would need the shift cables and maybe the shifter. My buddy just put an Isuzu 5spd in his 86GT and the 4sp shifter just didn't work because it wouldn't go into 5th and reverse. You will also need the mounting brackets for the tranny you are putting in. The slave look different, but either would work, but if you have the slave to the Isuzu I would use it,I did. The reverse light won't work though because the 4spd used a lever in the shifter to turn them on and the Isuzu has a plug on the tranny to make them come on. My 86SE V6 4spd had a couple wires coming off the speedo sensor that plugged right into the Isuzu and work fine. Maybe yours has the extra wires just hanging there too. If you put in this Isuzu, you will not know how to act. It shifts so smooth, like a hot knife through warm butter. <p>BOSTITCH, the Isuzu tranny is in the 85-88 4 cylinder Fieros. My 88 coupe has one behind the 2.8 V6 I transplanted. 
Z||000003||BOSTITCH||08-24-99||08:20 PM||||Thanx now Ive just got to find one.
Z||000004||Kage86GT4SP||08-25-99||12:16 AM||||Thanks, SCCA.. I appreciate it.  I'll get that stuff out of the car real soon, and get the show on the road.<p>K
